# Why: Filter `deleted-account@<host>` (orphan-envelope receiver) and
#      `serviceaccount@<host>` (legacy service account) out of the /admin/users
#      list. These two rows are load-bearing Documenso plumbing — they exist
#      to receive orphaned envelopes during user-deletion and to enforce the
#      impersonation-block, respectively. They must not be deleted or edited
#      from the admin UI. Their presence in /admin/users confuses admins into
#      thinking they're real users that need attention.
#
#      See `memory/system_service_accounts.md` for the full reasoning + the
#      original incident where one was almost deleted.
#
#      The filter wraps upstream's existing OR whereClause (name/email LIKE
#      search) inside an AND with a `notIn` sub-clause excluding the two
#      service-account email addresses. The service-account email getters
#      live in @documenso/lib/server-only/user/service-accounts/* and are
#      derived from the NEXT_PUBLIC_WEBAPP_URL host (so they don't drift
#      across environments).
#
# Why-not-additive: The filter applies to the existing `findUsers` query
#      function. There's no extension point (no callback, no query option)
#      where we could inject a filter from `packages/bizrethink/`. Inline
#      patch of the query builder is unavoidable.
#
# Upstream-merge-fragility: LOW. The patch wraps upstream's `OR` whereClause
#      inside an `AND` with our `notIn` sub-clause. If upstream restructures
#      the search (adds role filters, new search fields, etc.), the wrapping
#      AND-shape stays the same and our `notIn` survives. The only fragility
#      risk is if upstream changes the function name or whereClause variable
#      name; current line anchors (lines 1-2 imports, lines 11-27 of the
#      whereClause) are stable across upstream's recent lint sweep.
#
# Status: APPLIED inline since 2026-05-11 (system-service-accounts memory
#         note + incident). Patch file backfilled 2026-05-25 to restore
#         additive-fork discipline before the stalled upstream merge.

diff --git a/packages/lib/server-only/user/get-all-users.ts b/packages/lib/server-only/user/get-all-users.ts
